---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Louisiana Credit Transfer Checker | Credits That Count"
  description="A free Louisiana credit transfer checker for students, parents, and counselors, built from official published sources. Check courses you took, or courses you are thinking about taking."
  hideNav
>
  <div class="hero">
    <div class="hero-inner">
      <p class="hero-state">Louisiana</p>
      <h1>Which of your credits count?</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Check courses you already took, or courses you are thinking about
        taking, against Louisiana's published transfer rules. Free.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="container">
    <section class="block">
      <h2>Let's get started</h2>
      <div class="pathgrid">
        <a class="pathbox" href="/students/">
          <span class="pathbox-title">I'm a student</span>
          <span class="pathbox-desc">Check your courses and plan what to take next.</span>
        </a>
        <a class="pathbox" href="/parents/">
          <span class="pathbox-title">I'm a parent</span>
          <span class="pathbox-desc">Help your student check before enrolling or paying.</span>
        </a>
        <a class="pathbox" href="/counselors/">
          <span class="pathbox-title">I'm a counselor</span>
          <span class="pathbox-desc">Join the counselor list and follow the counselor tools.</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
      <h2>Built for Louisiana</h2>
      <p>
        Credits That Count serves Louisiana students, parents, and counselors,
        and Louisiana is the first state we serve. Every check runs on
        Louisiana's own published sources: the Louisiana Board of Regents
        statewide common course catalog, the Louisiana Transfer Degree
        pathways, and each Louisiana college's published course listings.
        Whether the credits come from dual enrollment in a Louisiana high
        school, a Louisiana community college, or a university across the
        state, the answer comes from the same public record Louisiana colleges
        publish.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
      <h2>Guidance you can verify, line by line</h2>
      <p>
        Every answer is built from official published sources: the Louisiana
        Board of Regents Course Articulation Matrix, the statewide common
        course catalog, college catalogs, and published admission standards,
        each dated and edition stamped so you can check the source
        behind any answer.
      </p>
      <p>
        This is guidance, not an official ruling. Only the receiving college
        makes the final decision on how a credit applies, and requirements
        can change. The checker states what the published sources say today,
        and names its sources so you can verify every line with the
        college.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
      <h2>About Credits That Count</h2>
      <p>
        Credits That Count is a free Louisiana credit transfer checker built
        by Credit Transfer Pros, former and current higher education
        administrators with experience in college student affairs,
        admissions, and student success. Louisiana is the first state we
        serve, and every answer is built from published sources you can
        verify.
      </p>
    </section>

  </div>
</Base>
